        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161-a3-a1">

                <pb facs="0568" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg354"/>

                <head>Archbishop Darboy to Mr. Washburne</head>
                <p>I beg the minister of the United States to accept my thanks for the kind visit he
                    has had the goodness to make me in my prison, and to send the inclosed letter to
                    its destination by his secretary, who is going to Versailles.</p>
                <p>The address of the person to whom it is written will be found through his
                    excellency the apostolic nuncio, or the bishop of Versailles. If the person to
                    whom the letter is addressed has already started for Paris, the secretary of the
                    minister can destroy it, or bring it back on his return to Paris. </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. DARBOY, <hi rendition="#italic">Archbishop of Paris, from the prison
                            of Mazas</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 23,
                    1871.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d161-a3-a1-a1.xml" xpointer="d161-a3-a1-a1"/>
